{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The free wait was served in full. This was an on-demand booking with no scheduled_at, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait ran from the driver's arrival at 08:29:10 and expired at 08:34:10; the driver did not cancel until 08:35:30, i.e. 380 s after arrival and roughly 80 s past the expiry of the free wait period. The trip record's own free_wait block marks cancelled_after_free_wait as true. On POL-NS-21 the cancellation fell inside the window in which the driver may cancel for a rider no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-TRIP-05059].payload.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival that starts that wait is not merely the driver's word. The auto-arrival event at 08:29:10 is corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace: from 08:29:05 the fixes sit stationary at the pickup, the nearest fix is 6.55 m from the pickup point against the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and its reported accuracy of 3.0 m is inside the 25 m accuracy filter. That trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, with 100% coverage, 25 fixes at a 30 s interval and no gap longer than 30 s.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05059", "EV-TRIP-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-GPS-05059].payload.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both limbs of the POL-NS-23 contact obligation were met before cancellation. The driver sent MSG-05059-001 at 08:29:30 and MSG-05059-002 at 08:32:45, and placed an in-app call at 08:33:40 that rang 25 s unanswered — message and call, each before cancelled_at of 08:35:30. I disclose that the chat artifact is IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 on issue UNREAD_MESSAGE, but that impairment points the other way: POL-NS-23 requires the driver to have SENT a message and PLACED a call, not that the rider opened or answered either, and the delivery timestamps (08:29:31 and 08:32:47) confirm both messages reached the rider's device. No FULL_REFUND arises under POL-NS-23.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05059", "EV-CHAT-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-TRIP-05059].payload.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account is contradicted by the record rather than supported by it. The rider says the driver 'cancelled too fast' and that the rider 'did not even see his message'; the record shows 6 minutes 20 seconds of stationary waiting at the pickup, two delivered chat messages, and an unanswered 25 s in-app call before the cancellation at 08:35:30. That the messages carry no read_at is consistent with the rider not having opened them, which is the rider's own conduct during a wait the driver was entitled to end, and it is not a fact that voids the fee under POL-NS-21.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05059", "EV-CHAT-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The fee charged is exactly the fee the policy sets, so nothing in POL-NS-22's amount check is engaged. The payments ledger shows a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD, total_charged 5.00 SGD, fee_matches_policy true, policy_fee_sgd 5.00 and payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.0. Under POL-NS-22 a driver who cancels after the free wait is entitled to that 5.00 SGD as compensation for time and fuel, and under POL-GEN-03 the outcome for a standing no-show fee is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05059", "EV-TRIP-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-FARE-05059].payload.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the record excuses the rider's non-appearance. EV-ADVIS-05059-01, the traffic advisory for this trip, is MISSING: its admissibility status is MISSING, its weight_multiplier is 0.0, and under POL-GEN-02(3) a missing artifact carries no fact. There is therefore no item of evidence showing any external condition that kept the rider from the pickup or that would lengthen the wait the driver owed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05059-01", "EV-TRIP-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-GEN-26 is not engaged, so there is no open question to escalate. Every fact the no-show rules require is on the record: the arrival (08:29:10), the start and expiry of the free wait (08:29:10 to 08:34:10), the contact (two messages and one unanswered call), the cancellation (08:35:30) and the fee charged (5.00 SGD). In particular, the absence of a scheduled_at on this on-demand trip does not open a gap, because POL-NS-21 supplies the start of the wait for an on-demand trip — the driver's arrival — and POL-GEN-26 forbids inferring an outcome from the absence of evidence except where a rule says so.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05059", "EV-GPS-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-NS-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-24 does not assist the rider either. That clause requires the driver to have failed to arrive at the pickup by the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes; here the only arrival evidence is a verified arrival at 08:29:10, corroborated by the GPS trace, and the driver waited a further 6 minutes 20 seconds and attempted contact before cancelling. There was no arrival failure, and because a message and a call were both made there was no contact failure, so neither the full refund nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit that POL-NS-24 attaches to a contact failure is available on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05059", "EV-GPS-05059", "EV-CHAT-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The AI ruling is final here, which removes any argument for holding this case open. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold at which the AI ruling is final at any confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag (rider fraud_flags 0, driver fraud_flags 0), so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 confidence bar is not raised; and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling on a no-show final subject to those bars. Nothing on this record brings the fee within a human-review band.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05059", "EV-DPROF-05059", "EV-FARE-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the fee stands, POL-NS-25's repeat no-show referral is triggered and should be recorded: rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is present and stands at 3, and the rule applies once that count reaches 3 or more. This is a referral naming POL-NS-25 only — it never changes the ruling on this trip, and I do not put it forward as a reason to decide anything.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05059"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
